Request schema validation is invoked in the normal request lifecycle from **`lib/handle-request.js`**, and the actual routine that validates `params`, `body`, `querystring`, and `headers` lives in **`lib/validation.js`**.

Files/symbols that answer it:

1. **`lib/handle-request.js` — `handler` / `preValidationCallback` / `validationCompleted`**

   In `handler(request, reply)`, Fastify first runs any `preValidation` hooks:

   ```js
   if (request[kRouteContext].preValidation !== null) {
     preValidationHookRunner(
       request[kRouteContext].preValidation,
       request,
       reply,
       preValidationCallback
     )
   } else {
     preValidationCallback(null, request, reply)
   }
